kdoctools: do not prepend the install prefix to an absolute datadir

ECM's KDE_INSTALL_DATADIR_KF is already absolute in Nix builds, so
prepending CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX produced a doubled path. Linux builds never
hit the broken fallback because Qt also searches XDG_DATA_DIRS (which the
wrapper points at kdoctools' share directory), but macOS Qt ignores
XDG_DATA_DIRS, so meinproc6 fails with "Could not find kdoctools catalogs"
when generating man pages for packages built against kdoctools.

--- a/config-kdoctools.h.cmake
+++ b/config-kdoctools.h.cmake
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@
 
 #define DOCBOOK_XML_CURRDTD "@DocBookXML4_DTD_DIR@"
 
-#define KDOCTOOLS_INSTALL_DATADIR_KF "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${KDE_INSTALL_DATADIR_KF}"
+#define KDOCTOOLS_INSTALL_DATADIR_KF "${KDE_INSTALL_DATADIR_KF}"
